  {
    "id": "b7ae212d8b7966ea9e59f526941d6b7225729b2b",
    "individual_note": true,
    "resolvable": false,
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3958746902,
        "type": null,
        "body": "Fix in MR !26 (`584524ec5`), phase 7 of `docs/ongoing-projects/object-save-fixes-and-arm-pricing.md`.\n\nWhat the tests showed beyond the description above:\n\n- The iedit commit had the same fault through `copy_object_main()`: it wrote back the hash\n  links, sheath pointers and trap the object had when the edit began.\n- An edit copy shared `char_sdesc` with the live object and both freed it; the iedit commit of\n  a corpse ended in a double free.\n\nNot fixed by !26: the special abilities, spellbook and script a live object held before the\nsave are still dropped without a free. Two objects can point at one list (see the note on #29),\nso they cannot be freed at the save yet.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
        },
        "created_at": "2026-10-05T22:20:01.577Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-05T22:20:01.577Z",
