  {
    "id": "cc4d809183bd086c0bae3683f5d9d13fd0be2ecb",
    "individual_note": true,
    "resolvable": false,
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3969817902,
        "type": null,
        "body": "Closed by MR !26, merged on 2026-10-07 as merge commit `632b50242`. The plan's record is closed in\n`529fee05d`.\n\n- `584524ec5`: `overwrite_object()` says in one place what a target keeps when another object is\n  written over it. An editor copy and its commit no longer share or drop runtime fields, lists or\n  `char_sdesc`, and a new prototype takes nothing from its slot.\n- Review, `8e7b0b073`: renumbering moves live objects to the hash chain of their new rnum. Objects\n  and notice boards with no prototype keep NOTHING. Removing an object that is on no chain leaves\n  the buckets alone, and `delete_object()` frees the deleted prototype's strings and triggers.\n- Review, `dd9732777`: an OLC save gives a live object the new definition field by field where it\n  still held the old prototype's, and keeps what it made its own. Generated items, restrings,\n  marks, written pages and essence levels survive a save. The save no longer orphans the script,\n  a live target keeps its rnum, and container and carrier weights stay in step.\n\nFound on the way and filed: #31 (mail letters and forged notes with rnum 1). Still waiting on #29:\nfreeing the ability lists and spellbooks an OLC save replaces.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
        },
        "created_at": "2026-10-07T11:11:35.973Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-07T11:11:35.973Z",
